    {
        "content": "<p>It works for me:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DivisionRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Nontrivial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSimpleModule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">End</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>with the <code>AddCommGroup M</code></p>",
        "id": 633048278,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryan Wang",
        "timestamp": 1792424968
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Alright, this is stupid enough <span aria-label=\"clown\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f921\" role=\"img\" title=\"clown\">:clown:</span> <code>variable (R)</code> brings overlapped instances. Making it variable (R : Type*) would work. The thing that actually annoyed me turns out to be another instance <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/SimpleModule/Basic.html#Module.End.instDivisionRing\">Module.End.instDivisionRing</a> where <code>[DecidableEq (Module.End R M)]</code> is needed. Thanks anyway!</p>",
        "id": 633062669,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1792427838
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"1097608\">Jiaxi Mo</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/.60IsSimpleModule.60.20instance.20failure/near/633062669\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>instance <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/SimpleModule/Basic.html#Module.End.instDivisionRing\">Module.End.instDivisionRing</a> where <code>[DecidableEq (Module.End R M)]</code> is needed.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This looks like a bad design, why are we requiring <code>DecidableEq</code> if it's noncomputable anyways?</p>",
        "id": 633066392,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1792428607
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I pointed out a similar confusing design earlier <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/44141\">#44141</a>, but didn't get any approval or disapproval.</p>",
        "id": 633067443,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiaxi Mo",
        "timestamp": 1792428821
    }
]